target/
mutants.out*/
*.wasm

# Deliberately NOT committed. Rust wasm builds are not bit-reproducible across machines
# by default, so committing one would invite a reproducibility claim we cannot honor.
# What is committed instead is a receipt: releases/*.json records the wasm sha256 next
# to the deployed contract id, and a test asserts that hash against what the network
# reports for the deployed contract. Anyone can pull the deployed bytes themselves with
# `stellar contract fetch --id C... --out-file`, which is a better source than our tree.
